  "text": "Recipe: Collard Greens Patra\nCreator: Kusum Dhairyawan\nCategory: Patra\nIngredients: Besan (chickpea flour), water, tamarind paste, green chili, ginger, garlic, cilantro, turmeric, hing (asafoetida), ajwain (carom seeds), salt, date sugar, ENO, collard leaves\nCooking methods: steam\nInstructions: Combine these together, along with water to make a thick batter for coating collard leaves:\n- Besan (chickpea flour) - 3 cups\n- 1 Tbsp tamarind paste (not from concentrate) - homemade by soaking tamarind and squeezing the pulp\n- 1 green chili (finely chopped), 1/2 inch ginger (finely grated), 2 cloves of garlic (grated, optional), a handful of cilantro (finely chopped)\n- Spices - turmeric, a pinch of hing (asafoetida), 1/2 tsp ajwain (carom seeds), salt (optional, to taste) and 1 tsp date sugar, and a pinch of ENO\n\nPATRA\n- Wash and dry collard leaves. Then remove the stems (the central ribs); use stems in a separate recipe.\n- Lay down a leaf on a flat surface. Coat it with thick batter from top to bottom. Then lay another leaf over the first leaf (coated with batter). Coat the second leaf with batter. Optionally, we may lay down a third leaf on top of the second leaf and coat it with batter - it depends on the size of leaves. Then roll them together like a spring roll.\n- Steam the rolls in a steamer for 30 mins. Insert a knife to check - if it comes out clean, that means the rolls are cooked thoroughly.\n- Let it cool completely before cutting into slices as shown in pic.\n- Serve with Green Chutney or Sweet Chutney.\nNotes: Use stems in a separate recipe. Tamarind paste (not from concentrate) - homemade by soaking tamarind and squeezing the pulp. Garlic (grated, optional). Salt (optional, to taste). Optionally, we may lay down a third leaf on top of the second leaf and coat it with batter - it depends on the size of leaves.",
